---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { projects, site } from "../../data/site";
import Cta from "../../components/Cta.astro";
import DataRows from "../../components/DataRows.astro";
import Flow from "../../components/Flow.astro";
import Manifest from "../../components/Manifest.astro";
import Doc from "../../layouts/Doc.astro";

const stencil = projects[2];

const toc = [
  { id: "problem", label: "01  THE PROBLEM" },
  { id: "architecture", label: "02  ARCHITECTURE" },
  { id: "data", label: "03  DATA MODEL" },
  { id: "stack", label: "04  STACK" },
];

const meta = [
  { k: "PRODUCT", v: "Stencil" },
  { k: "ROLE", v: "Everything" },
  { k: "TENANCY", v: "Row level security" },
  { k: "STACK", v: "Next.js · Supabase" },
  { k: "DATA", v: "Postgres" },
];

// No API tier of its own: the client talks to Postgres through Supabase, and the
// database decides what it is allowed to see.
const flow = [
  { name: "CLIENT", note: "next.js", lit: true },
  { name: "SUPABASE", note: "typed client" },
  { name: "RLS", note: "35 policies" },
  { name: "POSTGRES", note: "source of truth", lit: true },
];

const tables = [
  [
    "inquiries",
    "Seven states. The funnel is the product, so the states earn their own type rather than living as booleans.",
  ],
  [
    "bookings",
    "Its own five-state life, linked to the enquiry that produced it but surviving that enquiry being deleted.",
  ],
  [
    "clients",
    "Deduplicated on a generated, digits-only copy of the phone number, indexed per artist.",
  ],
  [
    "payments",
    "Integer cents, checked positive, with the method recorded as cash, transfer, card or other. Money is recorded here, not processed.",
  ],
  [
    "reminders",
    "One row per intended message with a scheduled time and a pending, sent or failed status, so a message that never went is visible rather than assumed.",
  ],
];

const manifest = [
  { label: "CLIENT", items: "Next.js · React · Tailwind · shadcn" },
  { label: "FORMS", items: "react-hook-form · Zod" },
  { label: "DATA", items: "Postgres · Supabase · RLS" },
  { label: "SERVICES", items: "Resend · Vercel · next-intl" },
];
---

<Doc
  title={`Stencil case study · ${site.name}`}
  description="How Stencil was built: thirty-five row level security policies instead of application filters, and constraints that make an invalid row unreachable."
  ogType="article"
  label="CASE STUDY 03 / STENCIL"
  back={{ href: "/work", label: "WORK INDEX" }}
  meta={meta}
  tocTitle="Contents"
  toc={toc}
>
  <Fragment slot="headline">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-[26px]">OWN PRODUCT &nbsp;·&nbsp; IN PRODUCTION &nbsp;·&nbsp; 2026</div>
    <h1
      class="max-w-[820px] text-[clamp(44px,6vw,84px)] leading-[0.96] font-medium tracking-[-0.04em]"
    >
      <span class="line"><span data-line class="block">The database is</span></span>
      <span class="line"
        ><span data-line class="block">the <span class="text-mint">application</span>.</span></span
      >
    </h1>
  </Fragment>

  <div data-mask slot="banner" class="overflow-hidden border-b border-line bg-panel">
    <Image
      src={stencil.shot}
      alt="Stencil request pipeline"
      widths={[900, 1400, 1900]}
      sizes="100vw"
      class="block h-[520px] w-full object-cover object-left-top"
    />
  </div>

  <section id="problem" class="scroll-mt-[90px]">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-5">01&nbsp;&nbsp;THE PROBLEM</div>
    <h2 data-reveal class="text-[34px] leading-[1.12] font-medium tracking-[-0.025em]">
      A tattoo studio is several businesses sharing a calendar.
    </h2>
    <p data-reveal class="mt-[22px] text-lg leading-[1.65] text-mute">
      Artists take their own enquiries, quote their own work, keep their own clients and their own
      income, and share a studio, a diary and a front desk. Software that treats the studio as one
      account gets the calendar right and the money wrong. Software that treats each artist as an
      island cannot show the studio a week.
    </p>
    <p data-reveal class="mt-[18px] text-lg leading-[1.65] text-mute">
      So the question is not what the screens look like. It is who is allowed to see which row, and
      whether that answer is enforced somewhere a missing filter cannot undo.
    </p>
    <div data-reveal class="mt-7 border-l-2 border-mint bg-mint/5 py-3.5 pl-5">
      <div class="text-[17px] leading-[1.6] text-paper">
        The constraint I set: no query written in the app should be able to return another studio's
        row, even if I write it badly.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="architecture" class="mt-[70px] scroll-mt-[90px]">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-5">02&nbsp;&nbsp;ARCHITECTURE</div>
    <h2 data-reveal class="text-[34px] leading-[1.12] font-medium tracking-[-0.025em]">
      No API tier, on purpose.
    </h2>
    <p data-reveal class="mt-[22px] text-lg leading-[1.65] text-mute">
      A Next.js app talking to Postgres through Supabase, with no service of my own in between. That
      only works because the authorisation lives in the database: without row level security this
      shape would be one forgotten filter away from a leak, and I would have had to build the tier
      back. This is the opposite call to ClassPortal, where the domain was wide enough that a NestJS
      API earned its keep.
    </p>

    <Flow fig="FIG. 02.1 / SYSTEM" nodes={flow} notes={["AUTHORISATION IS A POLICY ON THE TABLE, NOT A CLAUSE IN A QUERY","13 TABLES, ALL WITH RLS ON, 35 POLICIES BETWEEN THEM"]} />
  </section>

  <section id="data" class="mt-[70px] scroll-mt-[90px]">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-5">03&nbsp;&nbsp;DATA MODEL</div>
    <h2 data-reveal class="text-[34px] leading-[1.12] font-medium tracking-[-0.025em]">
      Thirteen tables, and the database says no.
    </h2>
    <p data-reveal class="mt-[22px] text-lg leading-[1.65] text-mute">
      Every table carries its own policies, its own checks and its own foreign keys with the
      deletion behaviour spelled out. A booking outlives the enquiry it came from; a client outlives
      the payment that referenced them.
    </p>

    <DataRows rows={tables} />
  </section>

  <section id="stack" class="mt-[70px] scroll-mt-[90px]">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-5">04&nbsp;&nbsp;STACK MANIFEST</div>
    <Manifest rows={manifest} />
  </section>

  <Cta heading="Need multi-tenant data that cannot leak?" layout="inline" />
</Doc>
